WEBVTT

00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:11.760
This is Izakaya Nobu.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:16.490
It's an ordinary izakaya, but 
there is one extraordinary thing.

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:14.990
<b>Nobuyuki Yazawa (32)
 Owner of the izakaya "Nobu"</b>

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:24.600
Our front door opens into 
a parallel universe!

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.000
<b>Shinobu Senke (23)
 Waitress at the izakaya "Nobu"</b>

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.010
Isekai Izakaya

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.010
Japanese Food From Another World

00:00:28.510 --> 00:00:33.010
<b>After Work Tonjiru</b>

00:00:41.650 --> 00:00:43.660
<b>Eva (14)
Dishwasher at Nobu.
Resident of Ancient City Aitheria</b>

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:45.620
Nobody's coming.

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:48.480
There are no customers.

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:51.660
It's almost spring, but it's 
still really cold today.

00:00:51.970 --> 00:00:54.530
Maybe everybody just wants to stay inside.

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:57.800
Taishou-san seems kind of down.

00:00:57.800 --> 00:01:01.000
Yeah, I mean, as the owner of this place,

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:03.570
these kinds of days take a toll on him.

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:06.640
Let's close up. There's always 
going to be days like this.

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:07.540
Sure.

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:11.460
I put so much effort into preparing 
this because it's cold...

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:14.180
Eva-chan, have you gotten 
used to the work yet?

00:01:14.430 --> 00:01:19.680
Yes, both Shinobu-san and you are so 
patient when you teach me things.

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:21.690
Eva-chan, you're a quick learner though.

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:25.960
Sorry, that it's left overs, but 
there's a lot of it for you today.

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:29.560
I'm happy, but it's also 
really hard to accept it.

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:32.930
Taishou, I'll put away the banner.

00:01:32.930 --> 00:01:33.700
Right.

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:36.070
What happened?!

00:01:36.590 --> 00:01:38.550
Th-There's a person!

00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:42.570
Hey, are you okay?!

00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:44.570
Nikolaus-san?

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:47.730
F-Food.

00:01:50.170 --> 00:01:52.580
Ahh, so warm.

00:01:51.390 --> 00:01:54.360
<b>Nikolaus (24)
Palace Guard
Ancient City Aitheria</b>

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:54.360
You saved me!

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:57.220
Why were you collapsed 
in front of our place?

00:01:57.890 --> 00:02:02.380
The reason for that was something 
that happened yesterday.

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:09.180
I'm tired. That company 
commander is too gung-ho.

00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:12.930
You bastard! No apology 
after you ran into me?

00:02:12.930 --> 00:02:17.450
I-I didn't do anything. You're 
the one who ran into me.

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:21.840
<i>Those are ruffians from the 
Backeshof Trading Company.</i>

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:23.730
<i>Best not get involved.</i>

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:28.960
<b>Aaaaaaah</b>

00:02:27.740 --> 00:02:28.960
Good grief.

00:02:29.310 --> 00:02:30.920
Hey, cut it out!

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:34.720
Huh? What do you want? Got a problem?

00:02:35.110 --> 00:02:38.120
I'm a palace guard. Palace 
guards also have the duty

00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:42.370
of protecting citizens 
from ruffians like you.

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:45.240
H-Hey, this guy's a palace guard.

00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:48.610
<i>Now that they know that, they probably 
don't want further trouble.</i>

00:02:48.610 --> 00:02:50.940
Huh, that's nice.

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:56.610
Yeah, if we take down a palace 
guard, our reputation will go up.

00:02:56.950 --> 00:02:59.880
We'll play with you instead then!

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:00.880
<i>Huh?</i>

00:03:01.770 --> 00:03:02.880
<i>What?</i>

00:03:03.350 --> 00:03:04.410
Get him!

00:03:05.140 --> 00:03:06.110
U-Um...

00:03:06.110 --> 00:03:08.840
That sounds like a terrible night.

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:14.380
Yes. But the real trouble came later.

00:03:15.730 --> 00:03:17.960
There's someone amongst us here that

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:20.330
dragged our reputation 
through the mud yesterday!

00:03:20.770 --> 00:03:23.850
How can we be palace guards 
if civilians mock us?!

00:03:24.250 --> 00:03:25.980
<i>He's talking about me!</i>

00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:30.250
<b>Berthold (32)
 Company commander of the Aitheria 
palace guard, known as the "Devil"</b>

00:03:26.690 --> 00:03:30.260
What's the matter, Nikolaus? 
You don't look so well.

00:03:30.470 --> 00:03:31.970
I am all right, sir!

00:03:31.970 --> 00:03:35.110
However, sometimes you can 
be vastly outnumbered.

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:37.490
What should you do in such a situation?

00:03:37.490 --> 00:03:38.130
You idiot!

00:03:38.130 --> 00:03:41.890
On the battlefield, you're 
always vastly outnumbered!

00:03:41.890 --> 00:03:44.590
What good are you if you can't 
take on 5 or 10 people at once?!

00:03:44.590 --> 00:03:46.130
<i>Is he being serious?</i>

00:03:46.130 --> 00:03:49.150
This happened because you guys are lazy!

00:03:49.150 --> 00:03:51.030
The responsibility lies with all of you!

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:53.760
That's why all of you will 
stay late and train!

00:03:54.650 --> 00:03:56.430
Kill or be killed!

00:03:56.430 --> 00:03:59.380
I'm going to make you taste that hell now!

00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:01.050
Company commander, sir!

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:03.130
I am the one who besmirched our reputation!

00:04:03.130 --> 00:04:05.020
It will suffice if I alone stay late.

00:04:05.020 --> 00:04:09.290
Oh? So you're saying you're going 
to do the training for everyone?

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:10.650
That is correct, sir!

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:15.800
All right. Then you alone will 
stay late for the training.

00:04:16.290 --> 00:04:18.740
Poor Nikolaus-san.

00:04:18.740 --> 00:04:20.400
He was helping someone.

00:04:20.650 --> 00:04:23.730
The training... was hell.

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:29.170
But you know? I had a method 
to endure the hard training.

00:04:29.170 --> 00:04:30.170
Oh?

00:04:30.170 --> 00:04:31.900
What was that method?

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:34.020
That's...

00:04:37.370 --> 00:04:41.070
<i>My legs feel like they're lead.</i>

00:04:42.510 --> 00:04:44.540
<i>Equipment that heavy</i>

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:47.030
<i>is going to put an immediate 
strain on your legs.</i>

00:04:47.610 --> 00:04:51.690
<i>But this is all so that you won't 
have any regrets on the battlefield.</i>

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:57.280
<i>When it's tough, you have to 
think about the fun times.</i>

00:04:57.280 --> 00:04:59.700
<i>My fun times, that's when</i>

00:05:00.110 --> 00:05:02.610
<i>there's tasty stuff in front of me!</i>

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:05.410
<i>When you're this hungry, it's gotta be meat!</i>

00:05:05.410 --> 00:05:09.520
<i>At a time like this, the nourishing 
ginger pork would hit the spot!</i>

00:05:08.150 --> 00:05:12.960
<b>Sizzle sizzle</b>

00:05:09.520 --> 00:05:12.880
<i>It's perfectly filling without leaving 
any bad aftertaste in your mouth!</i>

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:20.940
What? He's laughing? I guess 
he can handle even more.

00:05:25.910 --> 00:05:27.600
<i>This is intense!</i>

00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:30.750
<i>This is something that 
you can't manage easily.</i>

00:05:30.750 --> 00:05:32.720
<i>This is all for you.</i>

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:36.890
<i>What you're carrying right now is 
the gravity of Aitheria itself!</i>

00:05:37.840 --> 00:05:39.520
<i>At a time like this...</i>

00:05:40.470 --> 00:05:42.890
<i>it's gotta be steaming taro!</i>

00:05:42.890 --> 00:05:45.920
<i>It's the perfect match for reishu!</i>

00:05:50.290 --> 00:05:54.220
U-Unbelievable! Am I dreaming?!

00:05:57.110 --> 00:05:59.610
This is the ultimate test!

00:05:59.890 --> 00:06:04.100
Nobody has ever survived this test!

00:06:05.310 --> 00:06:07.470
<i>Th-This is really tough.</i>

00:06:07.740 --> 00:06:09.230
<i>H-However...</i>

00:06:09.610 --> 00:06:11.340
<i>At a time like this...</i>

00:06:11.970 --> 00:06:14.120
<i>A steaming bowl of oden!</i>

00:06:14.990 --> 00:06:17.810
<i>A hot piece of daikon, completely 
soaked with the broth.</i>

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:17.820
<b>Steam steam</b>

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:19.810
<i>Hot konjac.</i>

00:06:18.680 --> 00:06:19.820
<b>Wibble wibble</b>

00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:23.330
<i>They're healing my weary bones.</i>

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:29.850
I... I can't believe this!

00:06:31.460 --> 00:06:33.100
Wh-What happened?

00:06:34.190 --> 00:06:35.960
I-Is something wrong?

00:06:36.410 --> 00:06:38.360
You can go home.

00:06:39.840 --> 00:06:45.350
Anyway, I managed to survive the training 
by thinking about the food here.

00:06:45.610 --> 00:06:48.410
But when I made it to the door 
of this place, I was so relieved...

00:06:48.410 --> 00:06:50.210
That's why I looked like that.

00:06:50.210 --> 00:06:52.480
Well, good work.

00:06:52.750 --> 00:06:55.850
When you're chilled to the bone, 
this is great for warming up.

00:06:55.850 --> 00:06:59.120
Thank you. I'm starving.

00:06:59.410 --> 00:07:02.910
Today's special, tonjiru.

00:07:01.230 --> 00:07:04.400
<b>Nobu's Special Tonjiru</b>

00:07:01.230 --> 00:07:04.400
<b>Let the hot pork soup
warm your entire body</b>

00:07:02.910 --> 00:07:03.990
Tonjiru?

00:07:05.850 --> 00:07:09.240
It's blinding! Wh-What is this soup?!

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:13.370
Pork! Daikon! Konjac! Taro!

00:07:13.370 --> 00:07:18.140
All the ingredients from 
my dream are in here!

00:07:18.140 --> 00:07:21.390
This bowl is literally heaven!

00:07:21.390 --> 00:07:25.150
It's hot. Please eat it slowly.

00:07:26.280 --> 00:07:29.650
Am I allowed to go? Am I 
allowed to go to heaven?

00:07:29.650 --> 00:07:30.760
Please do!

00:07:35.980 --> 00:07:37.520
Hot!

00:07:38.350 --> 00:07:41.580
<i>The warmth is radiating through my body!</i>

00:07:41.580 --> 00:07:42.900
<i>Next, the konjac!</i>

00:07:41.910 --> 00:07:42.910
<b>Wibble</b>

00:07:44.280 --> 00:07:46.540
<i>This one is hot and chewy!</i>

00:07:46.900 --> 00:07:48.270
<i>And next, the taro!</i>

00:07:50.270 --> 00:07:54.050
<i>It's got a sticky and soft texture that</i>

00:07:54.050 --> 00:07:57.420
<i>envelops this warmth that slowly 
travels to the stomach!</i>

00:07:57.790 --> 00:08:01.160
That's right, I forgot to 
have the all-important soup!

00:08:02.590 --> 00:08:04.880
<i>What is this sweetness?!</i>

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:08.100
<i>Unlike regular miso soup, this has fat.</i>

00:08:08.100 --> 00:08:12.750
<i>I see, this has the sweetness of the meat 
and vegetables permeating the whole thing.</i>

00:08:12.750 --> 00:08:16.660
<i>All the things are goddesses 
here to warm me!</i>

00:08:17.660 --> 00:08:20.370
Are you all right? Nikolaus-san?

00:08:21.380 --> 00:08:24.570
That was close. I almost passed out.

00:08:25.150 --> 00:08:28.720
<b>Steam steam</b>

00:08:25.910 --> 00:08:28.150
<i>This is a ball of warmth!</i>

00:08:28.150 --> 00:08:31.390
<i>And it's as filling as 
having a rice bowl dish.</i>

00:08:31.390 --> 00:08:32.670
<i>I love it!</i>

00:08:34.440 --> 00:08:36.120
I'd like another one, please!

00:08:36.560 --> 00:08:38.640
Here you go, another tonjiru.

00:08:36.760 --> 00:08:38.630
<b>Steam steam</b>

00:08:38.910 --> 00:08:41.910
If you're having more, you 
should try this stuff.

00:08:41.910 --> 00:08:43.500
What is that?

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:45.040
It's shichimi chili.

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:49.550
It's a mixed seasoning that 
combines seven different spices.

00:08:50.120 --> 00:08:52.010
<b>A blend of seven kinds
of herbs and spices</b>

00:08:50.140 --> 00:08:52.010
<b>Shichimi Chili</b>

00:08:50.550 --> 00:08:53.020
So that's why it's called that.

00:08:56.910 --> 00:08:58.970
This tingle in the nose.

00:08:58.970 --> 00:09:03.200
It does remind me of some sort 
of mustard, but this scent is...

00:09:04.890 --> 00:09:06.360
What is this?!

00:09:06.360 --> 00:09:09.860
It's completely different than 
the slow build-up from before!

00:09:09.860 --> 00:09:12.260
The sweetness embedded in 
the soup and the spiciness

00:09:12.260 --> 00:09:15.900
elevate each other and it makes 
your body hot in one go!

00:09:15.900 --> 00:09:18.000
I've never tasted anything 
like this before, Taishou!

00:09:20.140 --> 00:09:21.700
What's the matter, Taishou?

00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:23.500
Did something good happen?

00:09:24.020 --> 00:09:26.720
Huh? Not really.

00:09:27.650 --> 00:09:29.270
I was just thinking.

00:09:30.010 --> 00:09:32.280
Even if they have a really rough day,

00:09:32.820 --> 00:09:37.580
customers come here and eat my food 
at night and they look happy.

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:41.020
I was thinking that that 
is an amazing thing.

00:09:42.030 --> 00:09:43.710
What are you talking about?

00:09:44.090 --> 00:09:47.570
I'm the one who's being saved by this food.

00:09:47.570 --> 00:09:49.310
I'm counting on you.

00:09:51.670 --> 00:09:52.310
All right.

00:09:52.660 --> 00:09:56.570
Wow, Nikolaus-san, you 
helped Taishou-san, too.

00:09:56.570 --> 00:10:00.830
Really. I hope tomorrow will be a 
good day for you, Nikolaus-san.

00:10:00.830 --> 00:10:02.820
Huh? Did I do something?

00:10:04.930 --> 00:10:08.210
On a night like this, 
I'd like to go to Nobu,

00:10:08.720 --> 00:10:12.720
but I have to go home and come 
up with a new training plan.

00:10:13.050 --> 00:10:16.620
I never expected that incompetent 
Nikolaus to endure so much.

00:10:20.770 --> 00:10:26.320
Starting tomorrow, the training will 
be double, no, five times as much.

00:10:29.200 --> 00:10:31.290
Next up, we've got Nobu Plus.

00:10:31.190 --> 00:10:33.020
<b>Nobu</b>

00:10:33.420 --> 00:10:35.030
<b>Nobu</b>

00:10:35.030 --> 00:10:41.000
<b>Tameikesanou</b>

00:10:35.040 --> 00:10:38.320
Government buildings and offices for the big 
companies line the streets of Tameikesanou.

00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:41.010
We're just outside Tameikesanou station.

00:10:41.010 --> 00:10:43.560
That side is Akasaka.

00:10:41.020 --> 00:10:45.690
<b>Kenichi Nagira</b>

00:10:43.560 --> 00:10:48.810
That's fine and all, but a place 
that specializes in tonjiru?

00:10:46.090 --> 00:10:49.130
<b>Tonjiru Restaurant</b>

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:50.080
That doesn't exist.

00:10:50.080 --> 00:10:51.670
There is a good place.

00:10:51.570 --> 00:10:56.090
<b>Narrator
 Teiyu Ichiryusai</b>

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:54.450
Kenichi Nagira is going to go around the bars

00:10:54.450 --> 00:10:58.150
here to find the amazing 
dishes featured in "Nobu".

00:10:56.450 --> 00:10:58.580
<b>Kenichi Nagira's search for the "Nobu" bar</b>

00:10:59.450 --> 00:11:01.270
Tonjiru, tonkatsu?

00:11:02.370 --> 00:11:04.240
<b>Tonkatsu   Masamune</b>

00:11:02.380 --> 00:11:03.410
Tonkatsu, huh?

00:11:03.410 --> 00:11:04.240
See here?

00:11:04.290 --> 00:11:08.320
<b>Kenichi Nagira
 Born in Tokyo's Ginza. Made his debut in 1970 as a folk singer.
 Since then, he's been active as an actor, celebrity, essayist.
 Has been in multiple shows that take place in bars or Shitamachi.</b>

00:11:05.040 --> 00:11:06.410
I think they might have it.

00:11:06.430 --> 00:11:07.570
You've got to try it here!

00:11:07.570 --> 00:11:08.140
Let's go in then?

00:11:08.140 --> 00:11:08.870
Sure!

00:11:10.990 --> 00:11:13.980
Masamune is a hugely popular place 
specializing in Japanese Mochibuta pork.

00:11:11.160 --> 00:11:13.960
<b>Tameikesanou - Tonjiru</b>

00:11:13.980 --> 00:11:14.720
Welcome.

00:11:14.720 --> 00:11:19.310
I'm going to ask something unrelated, 
but do you have tonjiru?

00:11:17.270 --> 00:11:21.490
<b>Tonkatsu  Masamune
 Owner Satou Makoto-san</b>

00:11:17.720 --> 00:11:19.890
Do you have tonjiru?

00:11:19.310 --> 00:11:19.980
We do.

00:11:19.980 --> 00:11:20.670
You do?

00:11:20.670 --> 00:11:21.100
Yes.

00:11:21.490 --> 00:11:24.800
Just that is something, so whatever 
pork cutlet you recommend.

00:11:24.800 --> 00:11:25.350
Yes, please!

00:11:25.350 --> 00:11:26.610
Then I heartily recommend the sirloin.

00:11:26.610 --> 00:11:29.050
Then that, and the tonjiru.

00:11:29.050 --> 00:11:31.250
Oh, and that brown stuff that foams.

00:11:31.250 --> 00:11:32.730
You're always like that.

00:11:31.550 --> 00:11:32.530
Ah, understood.

00:11:32.530 --> 00:11:33.370
Thank you.

00:11:34.080 --> 00:11:35.650
A whatsontap!

00:11:35.940 --> 00:11:37.140
They have Echigo no Aki.

00:11:37.140 --> 00:11:38.430
That's what they have at Nobu's.

00:11:38.430 --> 00:11:40.210
Isn't the label on the wrong side?

00:11:40.210 --> 00:11:41.490
Who cares?!

00:11:43.280 --> 00:11:44.510
It's hard to drink like this.

00:11:46.150 --> 00:11:47.850
That meat is so thick!

00:11:49.720 --> 00:11:53.130
The Japanese Mochibuta pork 
sirloin cutlet is being fried!

00:11:55.390 --> 00:11:57.600
You're already on your second beer?!

00:11:59.240 --> 00:12:02.230
This sound, it's so amazing!

00:12:03.390 --> 00:12:07.390
So this surface here, onto 
this surface, you squeeze.

00:12:03.940 --> 00:12:04.870
Yes.

00:12:07.860 --> 00:12:10.740
First, it's already really 
delicious just like that.

00:12:10.740 --> 00:12:11.300
Really?

00:12:11.300 --> 00:12:11.820
Yes.

00:12:12.130 --> 00:12:15.200
Their signature meat dish
 is soft and juicy!

00:12:15.200 --> 00:12:16.350
This is good.

00:12:17.180 --> 00:12:19.010
The soy sauce doesn't really 
get in the way, you know?

00:12:19.010 --> 00:12:19.760
I see!

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:20.390
I see.

00:12:20.390 --> 00:12:21.150
Yes.

00:12:22.240 --> 00:12:24.730
Apparently their soy sauce has 
also been painstakingly selected!

00:12:26.330 --> 00:12:29.610
How many whatsontaps
are you going for?

00:12:31.270 --> 00:12:32.170
I can't stop.

00:12:31.930 --> 00:12:32.660
That's obvious!

00:12:32.660 --> 00:12:35.920
Finally, this restaurant's famous tonjiru!

00:12:35.920 --> 00:12:37.360
Here is your tonjiru.

00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:39.440
Oh, I forgot about that. 
This was the main dish.

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:40.860
Don't just forget!

00:12:41.500 --> 00:12:42.270
How is it?

00:12:42.270 --> 00:12:43.170
Good.

00:12:43.170 --> 00:12:47.250
We use the meat of the Japanese 
Mochibuta pork for this.

00:12:47.250 --> 00:12:50.110
You're not just using any scrap or whatever,

